            "review_title": "Review at Chuc Linh",
            "review_text": "Sheryl A\nLiverpool, United Kingdom426 contributions\n0\nGood flavourful Vietnamese food\nMar 2014 • Couples\nAte here twice - had dinner - Chicken, chili, lemongrass (80k VND) with rice (25k)/fries(40k) (very tasty) with 2 x spiced-ginger teas (15k each). Food had great flavour - fries tasted buttery - yummy! Also had some cakes to go - chocolate cup (10k), huge danish (20k), banana/chocolate cake (12k) - all lovely. Also had lunch with Tuna sandwiches (70k) and although a little expensive for its size - it was nice. It is a narrow (seats at one side) typical Hanoi restaurant - clean and tidy. Good flavours - friendly service - reasonable prices for Hanoi.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten March 9, 2014",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
